  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the following system of equations:&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math></p><p>where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> are real constants. Then the system of equations :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "s8r1h",
      "text": "has a unique solution when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "622dS",
      "text": "has no solution for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8RQTc",
      "text": "has infinite number of solutions when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8baCL",
      "text": "has a unique solution for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
